  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 1257 PM CDT SUN SEP 13 2026\n\nThe weak upper-level trough continues to push off to the east,\ntaking these welcomed rain chances with it. In turn, upper-level\nridging is already beginning to establish itself across the\nsoutheast. By this time tomorrow, the apex of this building ridge\nwill have firmly established itself over Tennessee, decreasing\nour rain chances through the week significantly. Rain chances\nwill generally be low (<10%), with any isolated shower or storm\nbeing diurnally driven in the afternoon hours.\n\nAfternoon high temperatures will also quickly rebound by Monday,\nwith highs returning to the mid and upper-90s. While afternoon\nheat index values will generally reach above 100 degrees, no heat\nheadlines are anticipated given the lack of higher humidity. This\nwill be the forecast trend into next weekend, as very little\nmovement is expected from the upper-level ridge over the next\nfive days.\n\n/44/",
